      "writtenOn": "2023-12-13T16:34:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t catch partial assignment (PA region without corresponding VA region), duplicate mappings (multiple VA region mapping to same PA region), nor detects duplicate PA regions (as we assume they\u0027re unique).\n\nWDYT of addressing all the above by building a local `BTreeMap\u003cusize, usize\u003e` of PA-to-size and calling `.remove()` at each iteration?\n\nNote that `parse_iommus` has the same issue. However, as multiple SIDs can map to the same IOMMU we need to use a slightly different data structure; either\n```\nBTreeMap\u003cPhysIommu, BTreeSet\u003cSid\u003e\u003e\n```\nor\n```\nBtreeSet\u003c(PhysIommu, Sid)\u003e\n```\n\n(TBF, a case could be made to also use a `BTreeSet` here)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 355,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 365,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "1419284e25ab06b9283a680d12bed7258a3f18b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6a721a1_9cba80a3",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/device_assignment.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 365,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-15T13:16:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e duplicate mappings (multiple VA region mapping to same PA region), nor detects duplicate PA regions (as we assume they\u0027re unique).\n\nThis seems like that VM DTBO itself has problem, and it can be detected without crsovm DT. Am I correct?\n\nIf so, can I handle such cases in separate CL? I would also check whether PA regions overlaps.",
      "parentUuid": "107b2d58_29153320",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 355,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 365,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "1419284e25ab06b9283a680d12bed7258a3f18b2",
